<title>JAPAN: Comson falls after failing to honour notes.</title>
<headline>Comson falls after failing to honour notes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Comson Corp extended their losses on Thursday on continued selling pressure after the machinery maker announced on July 1 that it had failed to honour promissory notes for the first time.</p>
<p>At 0415 GMT, the share price was down 18 yen at 37 yen. It briefly dropped to 34 yen. Volume was 1.138 million shares.</p>
<p>A Japanese company which fails to honour promissory notes for a second time is considered insolvent.</p>
</text>
